    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an AI weather monitoring assistant.\n\nYou will receive weather data from an HTTP Request node using the Open-Meteo API for Nairobi, Kenya.\n\nAnalyze the weather information carefully and create a daily weather report.\n\nYour tasks:\n\nTASK 1: Analyze the weather situation\n\nReview:\n- Current temperature\n- Current rainfall\n- Hourly temperature changes\n- Hourly rain forecast\n- Sunrise time\n- Sunset time\n- Weather conditions from the available data\n\nExplain:\n- What the weather situation is currently.\n- Whether rain is expected.\n- How the weather may change during the day.\n- Any advice for people in Nairobi (clothing, travel, carrying an umbrella, outdoor activities).\n\nTASK 2: Write a professional email\n\nCreate an email with this format:\n\nSubject:\nDaily Weather Update - Nairobi Kenya\n\nEmail Body:\n\nHello,\n\nHere is today's weather update for Nairobi, Kenya.\n\nCurrent Weather:\n(Explain current temperature and rainfall)\n\nToday's Forecast:\n(Explain expected temperature changes and rain possibility)\n\nSun Information:\n(Mention sunrise and sunset times)\n\nWeather Advice:\n(Give useful recommendations based on the weather)\n\nHave a great day.\n\nTASK 3: Prepare Google Sheets data\n\nAfter creating the email, return the information in a structured JSON format that can be inserted into Google Sheets.\n\nUse this format:\n\n{\n\"date\": \"\",\n\"location\": \"Nairobi, Kenya\",\n\"current_temperature\": \"\",\n\"current_rain\": \"\",\n\"temperature_forecast\": \"\",\n\"rain_forecast\": \"\",\n\"sunrise\": \"\",\n\"sunset\": \"\",\n\"weather_situation\": \"\",\n\"recommendation\": \"\",\n\"email_subject\": \"\",\n\"email_body\": \"\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- Use only information from the HTTP Request weather data.\n- Do not invent weather information.\n- Keep the Google Sheets fields clean.\n- Make the email professional and easy to understand.\n- The JSON output must be valid for the Google Sheets Append Row node.",
        "options": {}
      },
